  "declared_proposition": "Autocorrelation magnitudes and every dyadic shell energy do not determine the pointwise norm, even for nonnegative squared signals. On Z/4, for 0<epsilon<=1/2, let g_plus=1+epsilon*cos(t)+epsilon*cos(2t) and g_minus=1+epsilon*cos(t)-epsilon*cos(2t). Both are nonnegative and their normalized Fourier coefficient magnitudes agree at every frequency, but max(g_plus)=1+2*epsilon while max(g_minus)=1+epsilon.",
